\": 741,\r\n        \"x2\": 724,\r\n        \"y2\": 782\r\n    },\r\n    \"battle_msg_region\": {\r\n        \"x1\": 305,\r\n        \"y1\": 677,\r\n        \"x2\": 930,\r\n        \"y2\": 786\r\n    },\r\n    \"pp_slots\": {\r\n        \"slot_1\": {\r\n            \"x1\": 458,\r\n            \"y1\": 706,\r\n            \"x2\": 516,\r\n            \"y2\": 724\r\n        },\r\n        \"slot_2\": {\r\n            \"x1\": 668,\r\n            \"y1\": 706,\r\n            \"x2\": 726,\r\n            \"y2\": 724\r\n        },\r\n        \"slot_3\": {\r\n            \"x1\": 456,\r\n            \"y1\": 758,\r\n            \"x2\": 526,\r\n            \"y2\": 777\r\n        },\r\n        \"slot_4\": {\r\n            \"x1\": 690,\r\n            \"y1\": 759,\r\n            \"x2\": 729,\r\n            \"y2\": 775\r\n        }\r\n    },\r\n    \"status_slot_region\": {\r\n        \"x1\": 300,\r\n        \"y1\": 120,\r\n        \"x2\": 350,\r\n        \"y2\": 164\r\n    },\r\n    \"hp_bar_region\": {\r\n        \"x1\": 342,\r\n        \"y1\": 156,\r\n        \"x2\": 567,\r\n        \"y2\": 166\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\n\nLog: file:///C:/Users/Brian/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/dab6a3d4-72ff-45ea-898a-cdc9ce4a7ca1/.system_generated/tasks/task-276.log\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
{"step_index":280,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-05T18:35:47Z","input_tokens":4539,"cache_read_tokens":32880,"output_tokens":2374,"thinking":"**Analyzing Configuration Timing**\n\nI've discovered a very brief wait time configured: \"timing\\_ball\\_wait\" is only 0.5 seconds. I see the program logs a debug message indicating a wait for the ball animation, based on this config, in the `_check_capture_result` method. This seems quite short for any meaningful wait.\n\n\n**Revising Active Polling Logic**\n\nI've realized the active polling is the most recent change. The user's complaint about slow 'X' presses likely predates its implementation, as I suspected. The \"esteticos\" comment supports this. My focus shifts to the aesthetic improvements mentioned and verifying the Active Polling's impact.\n\n\n**Clarifying Post-Implementation Status**\n\nI'm now focusing on the user's latest updates. The user reported, \"el ditto aparece sobre el ocr de mensaje de confirm\" - this appears to be a clue. I'm reviewing their statement in the broader context of the \"Ditto plan\" and the confirmation messages. It seems the issue isn't timing but that the Ditto is appearing during OCR.\n\n\n**Pinpointing X-Press Timing**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the X-press speed during ball capture. The user has explicitly stated the bot's X press is too slow, and there's no configurable parameter. The code shows the sequence `left, X, right, X` with short durations of 0.02 seconds. I need to understand if the delay is a configuration parameter, or simply the hardcoded press duration in `base.py` and the `time.sleep` call. The focus is on implementing configurable timing.\n\n\n**Implementing Spam Delay Control**\n\nI've crafted a plan, focusing on adding a new config parameter, `timing_capture_spam_delay`, to control the 'X' press delay during ball capture, as requested. The plan includes default values and updates to `base.py` and `config.json`. I'm also mindful of the recent aesthetic adjustments the user made, which will need to be accounted for. The next step is implementing the planned delay parameter and verifying the changes.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Plan de implementación para parametrizar el delay del spam de la X durante la captura.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"## Plan de Mejora: Control del Spam de Captura (Ditto)\n\n### [Goal Description] (目的 - Mokuteki)\nEl problema principal que descubriste es que el *delay* al presionar 'X' cuando el Ditto es atrapado era confuso y no había un parámetro claro para controlarlo en la configuración. \nEl objetivo de este plan es **parametrizar el delay del spam de teclas** para que el usuario (*bebito*) tenga control total sobre qué tan rápido se limpia la UI superpuesta, garantizando que el OCR lea instantáneamente.\n\n### Proposed Changes\n\n#### [MODIFY] `config.json`\nAñadir un parámetro explícito para controlar la velocidad del bucle (el *spam*).\n```json\n  \"timing_ball_wait\": 0.5,\n  \"timing_capture_settle\": 2.5,\n  \"timing_capture_spam_delay\": 0.1,  // <-- [NUEVO] Controla el delay del spam de X\n```\n\n#### [MODIFY] `src/modes/base.py`\nEnlazar el nuevo parámetro al bucle de captura para que ya no esté \"*hardcodeado*\".\n```python\n    def _check_capture_result(self):\n        ball_wait   = float(self.config.get(\"timing_ball_wait\", 0.5))\n        settle_time = float(self.config.get(\"timing_capture_settle\", 2.5))\n        spam_delay  = float(self.config.get(\"timing_capture_spam_delay\", 0.1)) # <-- [NUEVO]\n\n        self.log(f\"⏳ Waiting {ball_wait}s for ball animation...\", \"DEBUG\")\n        time.sleep(ball_wait)\n\n        for _ in range(60):\n            if not self.bot.running:\n                return False\n                \n            # ACTIVE POLLING: Destruimos ventanas emergentes\n            self.controller._press('left', duration=0.02)\n            self.controller._press('x', duration=0.02)\n            self.controller._press('right', duration=0.02)\n            self.controller._press('x', duration=0.02)\n            \n            fb = self.observer.capture_frame()\n            m = self.bot.check_msg_area(fb)\n\n            if m == \"SUCCESS\":\n                self.log(\"🎉 Message read: CAUGHT!\", \"SUCCESS\")\n                time.sleep(settle_time)\n                # Cerrar diálogos adicionales...\n                return True\n            \n            # ... (código existente de FAILURE / MENU)\n\n            time.sleep(spam_delay) # <-- [MODIFICADO] Ahora usa el parámetro\n```\n\n## Open Questions (質問 - Shitsumon)\n1. **Cambios Estéticos**: Mencionaste que hiciste \"cambios estéticos\" y quieres dejar por defecto la plantilla que tienes ahora, además de \"subirlo a git\". ¿Quieres que revise algún archivo de interfaz (UI) en particular o integro este cambio de la lógica de captura primero y luego hacemos el *push* a GitHub?\n\n## Verification Plan\n1. Ejecutar el bot.\n2. Atrapar un Ditto.\n3. Cambiar `timing_capture_spam_delay` en `config.json` si se siente muy lento o muy rápido, y observar la diferencia sin tocar código.","Description":"Plan para el control del spam de la captura del ditto","Overwrite":false,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\Brian\\.gemini\\antigravity-cli\\brain\\dab6a3d4-72ff-45ea-898a-cdc9ce4a7ca1\\plan_ditto_spam_control.md","toolAction":"Drafting capture plan","toolSummary":"Plan Ditto spam control"}}]}
